::PC_U03_L02_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U03_L02_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.TR.8
Question:
Which statement correctly describes the unit circle definitions?
{
~A. Sine is always the reciprocal of cosine.#Sine and cosine are coordinates, not reciprocals.
~B. Tangent is cosine/sine.#Tangent is sine/cosine when cosine is not 0.
=C. Cosine is the x-coordinate and sine is the y-coordinate.#Correct. A unit circle point is written as (cosine, sine).
~D. Secant is the reciprocal of sine.#Secant is the reciprocal of cosine.
}
